{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_51","type":"agent_message","text":"The refined fault test revealed a real translation mismatch. In the optimized Rust `.so`, LLVM inlined `create_state` into `confusion` and eliminated the 24-byte state allocation entirely; the C `.so` always performs that allocation and returns `-1` if it fails. I’m fixing the Rust export so this allocation remains an observable call boundary, then I’ll rebuild and rerun the entire suite."}}
